==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|encountre}} {{qualifier|obsolete}}
* [[incounter]] {{qualifier|archaic}}
* [[incountre]] {{qualifier|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
Recorded since 1297, {{etyl|xno|en}} {{term|encountrer|lang=fro}}, {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|encontrer||to confront|lang=fro}}, from {{term|encontre|lang=fro||against, counter to}}, from {{etyl|LL.|en}} {{term|incontra|lang=la||in front of}}  itself from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|in-||in|lang=la}} + {{term|contra||against|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-encounter.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|aʊntə(r)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To [[meet]] (someone) or find (something) [[unexpectedly]].
# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To [[confront]] (someone or something) face to face.
# {{context|ambitransitive|lang=en}} To [[engage]] in [[conflict]], as with an enemy.
#: ''Three armies '''encountered''' at Waterloo.''
#* Shakespeare
#*: I will '''encounter''' with Andronicus.

